#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0411 expect=skipped domain=GV
#note "THE GVSCAT ALL-FACET GATE (Fix #331 bucket 2, M2-D24 / M3-D18; pin owed by review S9 and authored by Fix #340). FRESH FIXTURE - this rule shipped with no scenarios at all. The GV dataset deliberately declares no GVSCAT column, so Requirements.Variables.All [GVSCAT] rejects the dataset and the rule is SKIPPED naming GVSCAT. Remove the All entry and the rule EXECUTES: since Fix #330 retired the injected var_exists guard, a bare empty(GVSCAT) is TRUE on every row of an absent column (absent = all-missing) and nothing else in the Check restricts the rows, so it would fire on EVERY row -- the flood the gate exists for. If this scenario EXECUTES (violation or silent pass), the gate has been removed -- escalate, do not rewrite the pin."
#library standard=sendig-genetox version=1-0
dataset GV label="Genetic Toxicology In Vivo"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col GVSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col GVTESTCD type=Char label="Test Short Name"
col GVTEST   type=Char label="Test Name"
---
S1 | GV | S1-001 | 1 | MNCELL | Micronucleated Cells
S1 | GV | S1-002 | 1 | MNCELL | Micronucleated Cells
---
